INT. BALLOON-ANIMAL CONVENTION, HOTEL BALLROOM - DAY

Fluorescent lights. Folding tables. Vendors sell latex in every color. A banner: "24TH ANNUAL TWIST-A-THON."

CHESTER "CHUCKLES" BOONSRI (40s, vest covered in pins) sets up a booth. Beside him, FLORENCE "FLO" OYELARAN (50s, jumpsuit) inflates a pink poodle. And at the next table, a nervous newcomer, DOROTHY PRUITT-AKINS (30s, accountant's blouse), clutches a pack of balloons as though they might go off.

CHESTER
Welcome to the circuit. First convention?

DOROTHY
Is it that obvious?

FLO
You're holding the balloons like a baby.

DOROTHY
I didn't know how else.

CHESTER
You squeeze them gently at the middle, like so.

He twists a long yellow balloon into a giraffe in four seconds. She stares.

DOROTHY
That's astonishing.

FLO
That's Tuesday.

CHESTER
Flo.

FLO
What? It's true.

A tall figure in a lime-green suit strides up to the booth. He is SIR REGINALD "REG" FAIRCHILD-BANGURA (60s, silk cravat, a monocle on a chain). He snaps his fingers.

REG
Chuckles! You owe me a sword.

CHESTER
Reg, I told you, the sword is in the shop.

REG
In the shop? Chester, it's a balloon sword.

CHESTER
It popped.

REG
It popped? The Duelist's Blade, my masterpiece, popped?

FLO
It was a good popping.

REG
(to Dorothy)
Young lady, you look like someone with an honest face. Has this man ever returned a borrowed balloon?

DOROTHY
I only met him ten minutes ago.

REG
Then he has had ten minutes to wrong you. Wait.

CHESTER
She's new. Be nice.

REG
I am always nice.

FLO
That's a lie.

REG
That's a compliment.

Dorothy takes a deep breath. Picks up a red balloon. Inflates it. Twists. Twists. Holds up a shaky, lopsided dog with three legs.

DOROTHY
Is this... okay?

Silence. Chester and Flo glance at each other. Reg pulls out his monocle and inspects it for a long beat.

REG
Madam. It is perfect. A lame dog is the soul of the craft.

DOROTHY
Really?

CHESTER
He's lying.

FLO
He's lying.

REG
I have never lied in my life.

CHESTER
He's lying.

Dorothy laughs. She sets the dog on the table, where it promptly rolls off.
